    "https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18351": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Mathematics",
      "description": "Careers at Bowdoin College | Assistant Professor of Mathematics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Mathematics Bookmark this Job Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. Online application for this position in Mathematics is only available through MathJobs. Visit https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/28670 to apply. Posting Details Posting Details Title Assistant Professor of Mathematics Posting Number F00313JP Department Mathematics Position Summary Bowdoin College’s Department of Mathematics invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment at the rank of assistant professor, beginning July 1, 2027. We seek a candidate specializing in probability and stochastic processes, with a preference for those whose scholarship or teaching connects to the mathematics of artificial intelligence and machine learning. The teaching load is two courses per semester. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term successful research. A Ph.D. in mathematics, applied mathematics, or statistics is expected by the date of the appointment. Bowdoin’s Hastings Initiative for AI and Humanity aims to critically examine, thoughtfully utilize, and ethically guide AI’s trajectory. A $50 million gift by Reed Hastings funds ten new faculty positions across disciplines; supports faculty in AI-related teaching, research, and creative work; sponsors workshops, symposia, and student research; and prepares the next generation of leaders to engage responsibly with the opportunities and challenges presented by artificial intelligence. Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks. At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity. Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html . In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available. Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions through MathJobs ( https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/28670 ). A complete application includes: a cover letter of up to two pages describing your experience and your short- and long-term goals in teaching and research. In your letter, please give specific examples of how your scholarship or teaching has engaged meaningfully with the mathematics underlying machine learning or AI – for example, stochastic optimization and sampling algorithms, high dimensional probability, diffusion models, statistical learning theory or teaching courses on the mathematical foundations of ML; a curriculum vitae; a research statement; a teaching statement describing your pedagocial experience and your approach to engaging and supporting students from a broad range of backgrounds; three letters of reference: two addressing research and one addressing teaching, submitted directly by the letter writers through MathJobs. Review of applications will begin October 8 and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000-$98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check. Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: https://www.bowdoin.edu . Posting Date 08/13/2026 Applications Accepted Until Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Online application for this position in Mathematics is only available through MathJobs. Visit https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/28670 to apply. Employment Category Full Time Year Round Job Start Date 07/01/2027 Job End Date Job Type Faculty Background Check Package Requirements Faculty/Administrative Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. Confidential arrangements will be made if you have a disability or require an accommodation in completing the application or in the interview process. Please notify Human Resources at (207) 725-3837 in advance so all necessary arrangements can be made confidentially. Staff & Casual contact: careers@bowdoin.edu Faculty contact: facultycareers@bowdoin.edu (t)207-725-3837 216 Maine Street, Brunswick, ME 04011 Bowdoin College is a member of the Diversity Hiring Coalition of Maine , and Live and Work in Maine . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18298": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Computer Science",
      "description": "Careers at Bowdoin College | Lecturer in Computer Science Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lecturer in Computer Science Bookmark this Job Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. At the time of application, you will be required to include information for three references, including name, title, email address, phone number and how you know the reference. Reference providers will receive an automatically-generated email from the application system. The email will provide them a link to upload a confidential reference letter on your behalf. You will not be able to view the reference letters but will be able to see how many have been submitted on your behalf. Posting Details Posting Details Title Lecturer in Computer Science Posting Number F00314JP Department Computer Science Position Summary Bowdoin College’s Department of Computer Science invites applications for a full-time, benefits-eligible lecturer-track position as Lecturer in Computer Science beginning July 1, 2027. The initial appointment will be for four years, with the potential for recurring multi-year reappointments and eventual promotion to Senior Lecturer, contingent upon successful review and reappointment. The teaching load is five courses per year and is expected to include a regular suite of core introductory-level courses (e.g. Intro to Computer Science, Data Structures ) as well as intermediate and advanced courses within the candidate’s area of expertise as opportunity and demand allow. As the primary focus for lecturer-track faculty is on teaching and pedagogy, the successful candidate will have a demonstrated history of pedagogical innovation and a commitment to keep abreast of advances in computer science pedagogy. An advanced degree (master’s or doctorate) in Computer Science or a related field is expected by the date of appointment. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching. The College offers opportunities for professional development, including a path to promotion to senior lecturer and eligibility for fully funded, one-semester senior lecturer sabbatical leaves, as well as support for teaching, grant-writing, artificial intelligence initiatives, computing software, and community partnerships in courses. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks. At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty, and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity. Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html . In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available. Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Please submit: 1) a cover letter; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a statement that describes your teaching philosophy and practice, including how you create learning environments that prepare students to interact constructively with a diversity of people, spaces, situations, and ideas; and 4) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letter writers will be automatically contacted upon submission of your application. Review of applications will begin January 19, 2027 , and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment without prior lecturer-track experience is $94,000 – $100,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check. Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: http://www.bowdoin.edu . Posting Date 08/27/2026 Applications Accepted Until Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants At the time of application, you will be required to include information for three references, including name, title, email address, phone number and how you know the reference. Reference providers will receive an automatically-generated email from the application system. The email will provide them a link to upload a confidential reference letter on your behalf. You will not be able to view the reference letters but will be able to see how many have been submitted on your behalf. Employment Category Full Time Year Round Job Start Date 07/01/2027 Job End Date Job Type Faculty Background Check Package Requirements Faculty/Administrative Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Teaching Philosophy/Principles Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? Indeed.com Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Ed Facebook Glassdoor Google Search HigherEdJobs.com InsideHigherEd.com LinkedIn Twitter MANP Maine Job Link LiveandWorkinMaine.com Employee Referral Bowdoin College Website Radio Ad TechMaine NCAA CASE Other If you answered Employee Referral or Other, please specify here: (Open Ended Question) Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. Confidential arrangements will be made if you have a disability or require an accommodation in completing the application or in the interview process. Please notify Human Resources at (207) 725-3837 in advance so all necessary arrangements can be made confidentially. Staff & Casual contact: careers@bowdoin.edu Faculty contact: facultycareers@bowdoin.edu (t)207-725-3837 216 Maine Street, Brunswick, ME 04011 Bowdoin College is a member of the Diversity Hiring Coalition of Maine , and Live and Work in Maine . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click